================================================================================
Title: Core-Collapse Supernovae from 9 to 120 Solar Masses Based 
       on Neutrino-powered Explosions  
Authors: Sukhbold T., Ertl T., Woosley S.E., Brown J.M., Janka H. 
================================================================================
Description of contents: light_curves/ (1.5Mb)
  Z9.6/
  W18/
  N20/
  - all of the succesfull explosion models from Z9.6, W18 and N20 engines were 
  post-processed with KEPLER until about 2.e7 seconds (~231 days) since the 
  explosion, to obtain approximate bolometric luminosities. Each table lists 
  time in days and log of bolometric luminosity in erg/s.
  These tables are 'trimmed' versions, as the original calculation had many 
  more points near the shock break-out and near the transition between 
  plateau and nebular phases. Please get in touch with us if you're 
  interested in those 'high resolution' tables. 

System requirements: All files are ASCII tables.

Additional comments: None.

================================================================================
